From e07b910a3e77ebf668a148145c52145e7ca1b237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor <20575526+VVlasy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:24:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover HomeKit event stream when it goes quiet

Temperatures only arrive as HomeKit push events. If the subscription dies
silently (or aiohomekit sets supports_subscribe=False after a disconnect
during resubscribe), temperatures freeze while /status still reports
connected.

Add a watchdog: after --event-stale-timeout seconds (default 3600, 0
disables) without events, resubscribe; if still quiet a window later, drop
the transport so aiohomekit reconnects, re-verifies and resubscribes. Each
step also polls once to catch up. /status gains events_stale and a
homekit_events block (last_event_at, seconds_since_last_event, recovery
counters).
---
